  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186083278,
      "id": "3fc81cba-b997-54bc-9e11-0a4ff130833e",
      "title": "Determining the Points Where the Tangent is Horizontal or Vertical"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "A curve is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx=4(t+3)^{5},\\,y=7t,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nDetermine the value of $t$ at which the tangent to the curve is vertical.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/value": "t=-2",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/id": "62fcc85a-91c9-5c97-96a9-d938a1896e64"
            },
            {
              ":answer/value": "t=4",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/id": "a552a2eb-1195-52a6-8f32-3de28ce64ba4"
            },
            {
              ":answer/value": "t=-3",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/id": "6a17e915-93ed-5b80-ac95-79341be2c596"
            },
            {
              ":answer/value": "t=-4",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/id": "ac9a5cd2-2305-5cca-abd8-46bf6fb36fc1"
            },
            {
              ":answer/value": "t=5",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/id": "1a317bc1-4f08-5664-978b-e2e3beea617e"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/id": "c2926e2c-ed31-5063-99df-59f9105859b9",
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "6a17e915-93ed-5b80-ac95-79341be2c596"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "The slope $m$ of a tangent line to a curve defined parametrically is given by\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent line is vertical if ${x}^{′}(t)=0$ while ${y}^{′}(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=20(t+3)^{4},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=7.\n$$\n\nSolving ${x}^{′}(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n20(t+3)^{4}=0\\,⟹\\,t=-3.\n$$\n\nNote that ${y}^{′}(-3)=7\\ne 0.$ Therefore, we conclude that when $t=-3,$ the tangent to the curve is vertical.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/id": "2a86f40a-7a12-590d-a7c1-1184bb9beddc"
    },
