  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186083278,
      "id": "3fc81cba-b997-54bc-9e11-0a4ff130833e",
      "title": "Determining the Points Where the Tangent is Horizontal or Vertical"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "A curve is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx=4(t+4)^{3},\\,y=6t,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nDetermine the value of $t$ at which the tangent to the curve is vertical.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/value": "t=3",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/id": "d549bbe6-90bc-5f84-a5ec-2c8a837c7523"
            },
            {
              ":answer/value": "t=-3",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/id": "4a143572-5b0c-5df4-a40d-eab017b1618c"
            },
            {
              ":answer/value": "t=2",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/id": "e4778ef1-c58c-56b4-b8bc-0cc0076a1812"
            },
            {
              ":answer/value": "t=-5",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/id": "108ae9fb-a384-50a8-9650-f63f5ebf6b34"
            },
            {
              ":answer/value": "t=-4",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/id": "a8a8bba7-2c27-5903-92df-d33189368553"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/id": "0d5379c3-5eca-5c8a-bd37-efbef442d5a6",
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "a8a8bba7-2c27-5903-92df-d33189368553"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "The slope $m$ of a tangent line to a curve defined parametrically is given by\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent line is vertical if ${x}^{′}(t)=0$ while ${y}^{′}(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=12(t+4)^{2},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=6.\n$$\n\nSolving ${x}^{′}(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n12(t+4)^{2}=0\\,⟹\\,t=-4.\n$$\n\nNote that ${y}^{′}(-4)=6\\ne 0.$ Therefore, we conclude that when $t=-4,$ the tangent to the curve is vertical.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/id": "dabf918b-371d-50f3-b4e6-5f53ed70928a"
    },
