  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186083278,
      "id": "3fc81cba-b997-54bc-9e11-0a4ff130833e",
      "title": "Determining the Points Where the Tangent is Horizontal or Vertical"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-1,\\,y=-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi .\n$$\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the tangent to the curve is vertical.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/value": "$t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ only",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/id": "610544be-f77e-53f2-8771-caba7f573899"
            },
            {
              ":answer/value": "$t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $t=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/id": "9db254bb-49ff-51f0-ac97-630567c5bd20"
            },
            {
              ":answer/value": "$t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $t=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/id": "a29bb614-2a23-5b0c-b56e-9ae12f138745"
            },
            {
              ":answer/value": "$t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ only",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/id": "8edfe1fa-2ae0-5270-b81f-c7349815f598"
            },
            {
              ":answer/value": "$t=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ only",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/id": "ae5d1368-ee7a-5d4d-b543-738d6564dc4c"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/id": "2fb03350-a58e-5fbe-a61a-fa569d291da9",
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "9db254bb-49ff-51f0-ac97-630567c5bd20"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "The slope $m$ of a tangent line to a curve defined parametrically is given by\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent line is vertical if ${x}^{′}(t)=0$ while ${y}^{′}(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSolving ${x}^{′}(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=0\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we note that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =3\\ne 0, \\\\ {y}^{′}(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) & =-3\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the tangent to the curve is indeed vertical when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $t=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/id": "d3c73a61-d3b4-5858-9a50-a90cc0ec4492"
    },
