  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186083278,
      "id": "3fc81cba-b997-54bc-9e11-0a4ff130833e",
      "title": "Determining the Points Where the Tangent is Horizontal or Vertical"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+8,\\,y=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-4,\\,2\\pi \\le t<4\\pi .\n$$\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the tangent to the curve is vertical.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/value": "$t=\\frac{5\\pi }{2}$ and $t=\\frac{7\\pi }{2}$",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/id": "cb2dcb0c-978d-5c44-b0b8-bde862bdb012"
            },
            {
              ":answer/value": "$t=\\frac{7\\pi }{2}$ only",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/id": "da163c4b-4a10-50de-a680-078cc145283a"
            },
            {
              ":answer/value": "$t=\\frac{5\\pi }{2}$ only",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/id": "beaef979-2064-5e38-a89b-c6603c411b3f"
            },
            {
              ":answer/value": "$t=\\frac{9\\pi }{4}$ and $t=\\frac{11\\pi }{4}$",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/id": "0c0cb094-3aac-53df-9c05-68280bdb93e7"
            },
            {
              ":answer/value": "$t=\\frac{9\\pi }{4}$ only",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/id": "c5a14c5f-671f-5b65-b84f-9356447f20a6"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/id": "601eff6f-0169-5663-8d76-03dfbe80ca75",
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "cb2dcb0c-978d-5c44-b0b8-bde862bdb012"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "The slope $m$ of a tangent line to a curve defined parametrically is given by\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent line is vertical if ${x}^{′}(t)=0$ while ${y}^{′}(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSolving ${x}^{′}(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=0\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{5\\pi }{2},\\frac{7\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we note that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(\\frac{5\\pi }{2}) & =-5\\ne 0, \\\\ {y}^{′}(\\frac{7\\pi }{2}) & =5\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the tangent to the curve is indeed vertical when $t=\\frac{5\\pi }{2}$ and $t=\\frac{7\\pi }{2}.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/id": "e06e2bd3-b069-5886-8e45-aa84a82e9939"
    },
